  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Broussochalcone A may interact with the CD276 antigen through a series of molecular targets. The compound is implicated in targeting Lysine-specific demethylase 2A, which in turn is a target of Cryptophycin G and Lyngbyastatin 2. These latter two compounds are also linked to the CD276 antigen, indicating a potential pathway where Broussochalcone A could influence the antigen through its interaction with Lysine-specific demethylase 2A. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, with varying degrees of support from different compounds. The evidence highlights a possible mechanism involving enzymatic targets and their downstream effects on CD276 antigen expression, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
